{
	"project": "Pydantic Adapter 100% Compliance",
	"description": "Fix all failing compliance tests in the pydantic adapter to achieve 100% coverage across all JSON Schema drafts",
	"tasks": [
		{
			"title": "Fix field name shadowing Python builtins (63 failures)",
			"steps": [
				"Read renderer.py and find _sanitize_property_name function",
				"Add a set of Python builtin names that shadow types: list, dict, str, int, float, bool, type, set, tuple, object, bytes, complex, frozenset, range, slice, property, classmethod, staticmethod",
				"Update _sanitize_property_name to rename fields that match these builtins (e.g., list -> list_, or list_field)",
				"Ensure the field uses Field(alias='list') to preserve JSON serialization",
				"Write unit test for the new sanitization logic"
			],
			"verify": [
				"Run: cd python/packages/adapters/pydantic && bun run compliance -- --draft draft4 --keyword refRemote",
				"All refRemote tests pass (no failures)",
				"Run: cd python/packages/adapters/pydantic && bunx tsc --noEmit (if applicable) or python type checks pass"
			],
			"passes": true,
			"id": "1"
		},
		{
			"title": "Fix additionalItems applicator scoping (3 failures)",
			"steps": [
				"Read renderer.py array/tuple handling code",
				"Find where additionalItems validation is implemented",
				"The bug: additionalItems should NOT look inside allOf/anyOf/oneOf for items keyword",
				"Per JSON Schema spec, additionalItems only interacts with items at the same schema level",
				"Fix the logic to check for items only at the current level, not in nested applicators",
				"The test schema has items inside allOf, additionalItems at root - root additionalItems should apply to ALL items"
			],
			"verify": [
				"Run: cd python/packages/adapters/pydantic && bun run compliance -- --draft draft4 --keyword additionalItems",
				"All additionalItems tests pass (no failures)",
				"Run: cd python/packages/adapters/pydantic && bun run compliance -- --draft draft6 --keyword additionalItems",
				"Run: cd python/packages/adapters/pydantic && bun run compliance -- --draft draft7 --keyword additionalItems"
			],
			"passes": false,
			"id": "2"
		},
		{
			"title": "Fix unevaluatedProperties uncle schema (2 failures)",
			"steps": [
				"Study the failing test case: nested unevaluatedProperties inside foo.properties with anyOf at root defining foo.faz",
				"The test {foo: {bar: 'test'}} should be VALID - only bar is present, bar is evaluated by foo.properties",
				"Check how Zod adapter handles this case (it passes) - compare zod/src/renderer.ts with pydantic renderer.py",
				"The issue: when generating code for nested objects, the adapter must not incorrectly flag properties as unevaluated",
				"Properties defined in ancestor applicators (anyOf at root) do NOT count as evaluated for nested unevaluatedProperties",
				"But the simple case (only bar present, bar in properties) should pass"
			],
			"verify": [
				"Run: cd python/packages/adapters/pydantic && bun run compliance -- --draft draft2019-09 --keyword unevaluatedProperties",
				"All unevaluatedProperties tests pass (no failures)",
				"Run: cd python/packages/adapters/pydantic && bun run compliance -- --draft draft2020-12 --keyword unevaluatedProperties"
			],
			"passes": false,
			"id": "3"
		},
		{
			"title": "Fix JavaScript pseudo-array handling (1 failure)",
			"steps": [
				"Read renderer.py tuple/items handling code",
				"The failing test: objects with numeric string keys like {'0': 'foo', '1': 'bar', 'length': 2}",
				"Per JSON Schema, 'items' keyword applies to arrays, not objects - the pseudo-array is an object",
				"Check if the adapter incorrectly validates objects against items schema",
				"The fix: ensure tuple/items validation only applies to actual lists, not dict objects",
				"Objects should pass through tuple schemas unchanged (no type constraint = pass non-arrays)"
			],
			"verify": [
				"Run: cd python/packages/adapters/pydantic && bun run compliance -- --draft draft2019-09 --keyword items",
				"All items tests pass (no failures)"
